{%- comment -%}
  Icon for #ka-rail (layout/theme.liquid), repeated vertically down the
  rail. Each of the 12 cases below is one letterform isolated from
  Santosh's multi-script 'ka' wordmark SVG (viewBox/path data extracted
  and cropped to each glyph's own bounding box via a headless-browser
  getBBox() pass, not hand-measured) - spells 'ka' across Kannada,
  Devanagari, Tamil, Telugu, Malayalam, Bengali, and Latin scripts, the
  same multi-script treatment PROJECT_CONTEXT.md's logo notes describe
  around the badge border.

  Two more glyphs (raster images in the original file) aren't included -
  their embedded PNG data came through corrupted (broken IDAT stream,
  confirmed via PIL) and couldn't be reconstructed. Ping Santosh for a
  clean copy of those two if they need to be added back in.

  fill="currentColor" on each path so #ka-rail's own color setting
  controls it, same as the placeholder dot this replaced.

  @param {number} index - which glyph to render, 0-11
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign n = index | modulo: 12
%}
